A menu item without an action no longer deadlocks: GPUI's `handle_menu_item` and `validate_menu_item` released the
platform lock only when the item's tag named an action, then took the lock again to put the callback back, so any other
tag hung the main thread on its own non-reentrant mutex. ngterm builds its AppKit menu bar itself (`macos.m`), so
`menu_actions` stays empty, and Edit's items, sent down the responder chain for WebKit, end at GPUI's app delegate
whenever a terminal has the focus. The lock is now released on both paths: the item validates as disabled and a click
does nothing. scripts/vendor-gpui.sh applies this to the verified crates.io archive.

--- a/src/platform.rs
+++ b/src/platform.rs
@@ -1504,9 +1504,9 @@
         if let Some(mut callback) = lock.menu_command.take() {
             let tag: NSInteger = msg_send![item, tag];
             let index = tag as usize;
-            if let Some(action) = lock.menu_actions.get(index) {
-                let action = action.boxed_clone();
-                drop(lock);
+            let action = lock.menu_actions.get(index).map(|action| action.boxed_clone());
+            drop(lock);
+            if let Some(action) = action {
                 callback(&*action);
             }
             platform.0.lock().menu_command.get_or_insert(callback);
@@ -1522,9 +1522,9 @@
